                                                                                
 Usage: opentide new [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                                
                                                                                
 Scaffold a threat, objective or rule from its template                         
                                                                                
 The new file gets a fresh UUID, today's date, your git author and the          
 catalogue's organisation, and is named the way opentide lint expects. Required 
 values nobody has chosen yet are placeholders, listed in the output: replace   
 them, then run opentide validate --file on the path.                           
                                                                                
╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ --help          Show this message and exit.                                  │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ threat     Scaffold a threat                                                 │
│ objective  Scaffold a detection objective                                    │
│ rule       Scaffold a detection rule                                         │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

 Examples
   $ opentide new threat --name "Credential Dumping"
